OL,3,GNEWSADebbie McGee joins walk for brain
OL,4,Atumour charity
OL,5,
OL,6,FAbout 250 people including Debbie McGee
OL,7,Fhave taken part in a walk for brain
OL,8,Ftumour patients and their families.
OL,10,FThe Walk of Hope took place on Saturday
OL,11,Fat the Chatsworth Estate, in
OL,12,FDerbyshire, to raise money for charity
OL,13,FBrain Tumour Research.
OL,15,FDebbie McGee became patron of the
OL,16,Fcharity earlier this year, after her
OL,17,Fhusband - magician Paul Daniels - died
OL,18,Fof a brain tumour 10 years ago.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,363,360,200,160,0,100
